#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:29
msgid "Set locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Ubuntu-Set-Locale.rst:5
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. If you are in a "
"minimal environment (such as a docker container), the locale may be "
"something minimal like ``POSIX``. We test with the following settings. "
"However, it should be fine if you're using a different UTF-8 supported "
"locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Ubuntu-Set-Locale.rst:10
msgid ""
"$ locale  # check for UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install locales\n"
"$ sudo locale-gen en_US en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ sudo update-locale LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ export LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ locale  # verify settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:34
msgid "Enable required repositories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:5
msgid "You will need to add the ROS 2 apt repository to your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:7
msgid ""
"First ensure that the `Ubuntu Universe repository <https://help.ubuntu.com/"
"community/Repositories/Ubuntu>`_ is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:9
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install software-properties-common\n"
"$ sudo add-apt-repository universe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:14
msgid ""
"The `ros-apt-source <https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-source/"
">`_ packages provide keys and apt source configuration for the various ROS "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:16
msgid ""
"Installing the ros2-apt-source package will configure ROS 2 repositories for "
"your system. Updates to repository configuration will occur automatically "
"when new versions of this package are released to the ROS repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Repositories.rst:19
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install curl -y\n"
"$ export ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/latest | grep -F \"tag_name\" | awk -"
"F'\"' '{print $4}')\n"
"$ curl -L -o /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb \"https://github.com/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/download/${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}/"
"ros2-apt-source_${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}.$(. /etc/os-release && echo "
"${UBUNTU_CODENAME:-${VERSION_CODENAME}})_all.deb\"\n"
"$ sudo dpkg -i /tmp/ros2-apt-source.deb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:39
msgid "Install development tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:41
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y \\\n"
"  python3-mypy \\\n"
"  python3-pip \\\n"
"  python3-pytest \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-cov \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-mock \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-repeat \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-rerunfailures \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-runner \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-timeout \\\n"
"  ros-dev-tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:56
msgid "Build ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:59
msgid "Get ROS 2 code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:61
msgid "Create a workspace and clone all repos:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:63
msgid ""
"$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_rolling/src\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/rolling/"
"ros2.repos src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:72
msgid "Install dependencies using rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Upgrade-Admonition.rst:5
msgid ""
"ROS 2 packages are built on frequently updated Ubuntu systems. It is always "
"recommended that you ensure your system is up to date before installing new "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Apt-Upgrade-Admonition.rst:8
msgid "$ sudo apt upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:76
msgid ""
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -y --skip-keys \"fastcdr rti-"
"connext-dds-7.7.0 urdfdom_headers\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_rosdep_Linux_Mint.rst:5
msgid ""
"**Note**: If you're using a distribution that is based on Ubuntu (like Linux "
"Mint) but does not identify itself as such, you'll get an error message like "
"``Unsupported OS [mint]``. In this case append ``--os=ubuntu:resolute`` to "
"the above command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:85
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:87
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at build or runtime. See the :doc:`guide <../RMW-"
"Implementations/Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work "
"with multiple RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:91
msgid "Install colcon mixins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:93
msgid ""
"$ colcon mixin add default https://github.com/colcon/colcon-mixin-repository/"
"raw/master/index.yaml\n"
"$ colcon mixin update default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:99
msgid "Build the code in the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:101
msgid ""
"If you have already installed ROS 2 another way (either via debs or the "
"binary distribution), make sure that you run the below commands in a fresh "
"environment that does not have those other installations sourced. Also "
"ensure that you do not have ``source /opt/ros/${ROS_DISTRO}/setup.bash`` in "
"your ``.bashrc``. You can make sure that ROS 2 is not sourced with the "
"command ``printenv | grep -i ROS``. The output should be empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:106
msgid ""
"More info on working with a ROS workspace can be found in :doc:`this "
"tutorial <../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-"
"Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:108
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling/\n"
"$ colcon build --symlink-install --mixin release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:115
msgid ""
"If you are having trouble compiling all examples and this is preventing you "
"from completing a successful build, you can use the ``--packages-skip`` "
"colcon flag to ignore the package that is causing problems. For instance, if "
"you don't want to install the large OpenCV library, you could skip building "
"the packages that depend on it using the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:118
msgid ""
"$ colcon build --symlink-install --packages-skip image_tools "
"intra_process_demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:123
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:125
msgid "Set up your environment by sourcing the following file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:127
msgid "$ . ~/ros2_rolling/install/local_setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:133
msgid ""
"Replace ``.bash`` with your shell if you're not using bash. Possible values "
"are: ``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:139
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:141
msgid ""
"In one terminal, source the setup file and then run a C++ ``talker``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:143
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:148
msgid ""
"In another terminal source the setup file and then run a Python "
"``listener``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:150
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:155
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:160
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:162
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:165
msgid "Alternate compilers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:167
msgid ""
"Using a different compiler besides gcc to compile ROS 2 is easy. If you set "
"the environment variables ``CC`` and ``CXX`` to executables for a working C "
"and C++ compiler, respectively, and retrigger CMake configuration (by using "
"``--cmake-force-configure`` or by deleting the packages you want to be "
"affected), CMake will reconfigure and use the different compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:171
msgid "Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:173
msgid "To configure CMake to detect and use Clang:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:175
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install clang\n"
"$ export CC=clang\n"
"$ export CXX=clang++\n"
"$ colcon build --cmake-force-configure"
msgstr ""

