#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:193
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:195
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with colcon as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's ``setup`` file. This way, your environment will "
"behave as though there is no Rolling install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:198
msgid ""
"If you're also trying to free up space, you can delete the entire workspace "
"directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.rst:200
msgid "$ rm -rf ~/ros2_rolling"
msgstr ""
